# Quasithin groups: minimal parabolics

Minimal parabolics over a fixed Sylow 2-subgroup provide the local subgroups
used in the subsequent pushing-up arguments. The elementary generation results
follow from McBride's lemma and the normalizer action on the family of
nonnormal unique-maximal overgroups.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*, combined
manuscript (1 March 2004), §B.6–B.7, pp. 112–120.
-/
